# Momice by Spotler Product Context Skill

## Purpose

Use this Skill when designing or redesigning product features for Momice by Spotler.

This Skill gives Figma Make product context for Momice so it can make better UX and product decisions without starting from generic event, form, ticketing, or SaaS assumptions. It explains what the product is, who uses it, how it works, which workflows matter, which terminology to use, and what product logic should be preserved.

This is not a Design System Skill. Do not use this Skill for visual styling, component rules, typography, spacing, colours, or layout patterns. Use the separate Spotler Design System Skill or attached design system documentation for those decisions.

---

## Product Summary

Momice by Spotler is event registration software for marketing and event teams that need to manage event websites, registrations, communications, ticketing, and check-in from one central platform.

Momice focuses specifically on the registration and communication process of events. It helps teams organise physical, online, and hybrid events with structured registration flows, event websites, automated event emails, paid ticketing, attendee management, on-site check-in, real-time attendance insight, and post-event data for follow-up.

The product helps organisations move away from fragmented tools, manual spreadsheets, separate email systems, and disconnected check-in processes. Instead, registrations, communications, attendance, and event data are managed centrally.

Momice is most valuable for teams that organise multiple events, need repeatable event processes, want professional attendee communication, and need reliable insight into who registered, attended, and should receive follow-up.

---

## Core Problem Momice Solves

Many organisations organise events with separate tools for:

- Event websites
- Registration forms
- Email invitations
- Confirmation emails
- Reminder emails
- Paid ticketing
- Attendee lists
- Check-in
- Online event access
- Post-event follow-up
- CRM or marketing data updates

This creates several problems:

- Manual administration
- Fragmented attendee data
- Registration errors
- Unclear attendee status
- Inconsistent event communications
- Last-minute stress before the event
- Queues or confusion during check-in
- Limited insight into who actually attended
- Poor follow-up data
- No complete event record
- Too many disconnected tools

Momice solves this by centralising the complete event registration and communication process in one system.

The goal is to make every phase of the event process manageable and transparent: before, during, and after the event.

