## Main Product Areas and Capabilities

### Event Setup and Websites

Momice allows teams to create a dedicated event website linked to registration and event content.

Event website capabilities:

- Dedicated event website
- Event information management
- Programme or agenda content
- Practical information
- Registration link
- Event format details
- Online access information
- Content linked directly to registration
- Support for multiple event types

Design implication:

- The event website is the central source of event information.
- It should be connected to registration and attendee communication.
- Avoid treating event pages as disconnected landing pages or PDFs.

---

### Registration Forms

Momice supports configurable registration forms that are directly linked to event data.

Registration form capabilities:

- Custom registration forms
- Attendee data collection
- Registration status tracking
- Plus-one management
- Waiting list support
- Ticket type selection
- Online or physical attendance selection
- Payment-related fields where relevant

Design implication:

- Registration is the backbone of the event process.
- Form responses should update attendee records and statuses.
- Avoid treating registrations as generic form submissions with no event lifecycle.

---

### Registration and Attendee Management

Momice manages attendees centrally.

Attendee management includes:

- Registered attendees
- Attendance status
- Registration status
- Plus-ones
- Waiting lists
- Ticket types
- Paid event status
- No-shows
- Online attendees
- Physical attendees
- Hybrid attendee groups

Design implication:

- Attendee status is a core object.
- Users need clear insight into who registered, who attended, who did not attend, and who is waiting.
- Capacity and status logic matter.

---

### Ticketing and Paid Events

Momice supports paid events and ticket types as part of the registration process.

Ticketing capabilities:

- Paid events
- Ticket types
- Payment provider integration
- Registration linked to payment
- Payment status
- Access logic based on ticket or payment status

Design implication:

- Ticketing is part of the registration flow, not a separate unrelated checkout.
- Payment status may affect confirmation, access, and check-in.
- Designs should support different ticket types and attendee statuses.

---

### Emails and Event Communications

Momice sends event-related emails from the platform.

Event communication types:

- Invitations
- Registration confirmations
- Reminder emails
- Access information
- Updates
- Post-event follow-up
- Segment-based emails
- Status-based emails

Communication logic:

- Emails can be triggered by registration status.
- Emails can be segmented based on attendee type, status, or event format.
- Communications should align with the event website and registration process.

Design implication:

- Event emails are part of the event lifecycle.
- Avoid treating emails as generic campaigns disconnected from registration status.
- Timing and status-based communication are important.

---

### Online, Hybrid, and On-Site Execution

Momice supports different event formats.

Event formats:

- Physical events
- Online events
- Hybrid events

Execution capabilities:

- Online access management
- Streaming platform connections
- Check-in app for physical events
- Real-time attendance tracking
- Separate communication for online and physical attendees
- Hybrid attendee management

Design implication:

- Event format affects registration, communication, access, and check-in.
- Hybrid events require different flows for online and physical attendees.
- Designs should not assume every event has on-site check-in only.

---

### Check-In App and Badge Solution

Momice includes a check-in app for physical events.

Check-in capabilities:

- Scan attendees upon arrival
- Search attendee list
- Register attendance
- Track attendance in real time
- Support badge or check-in solution
- Reduce queues
- Provide accurate attendance list

Design implication:

- Check-in is time-sensitive and operational.
- Speed and accuracy are crucial on the event day.
- Real-time attendance insight is a key outcome.

---

### Interactive Module

Momice can encourage attendee interaction through an interactive module.

Possible interaction contexts:

- Event engagement
- Questions
- Feedback
- Polling or participation
- Interaction during or around the event

Design implication:

- Interaction should be connected to event participation.
- Avoid treating attendee interaction as a generic survey unless the feature context specifies it.

---

### Insight and Optimisation

Momice provides insight into registrations and attendance.

Insight areas include:

- Registration count
- Attendance count
- No-shows
- Registration status
- Attendance status
- Event performance
- Event record
- Future event optimisation

Design implication:

- Reporting should help teams understand event execution and follow-up.
- Attendance insight is more valuable than registration count alone.
- Event records should support future improvement.

