## Important Product Objects and Concepts

### Event

A planned physical, online, or hybrid gathering managed in Momice.

### Event website

A dedicated website for event information, registration, access details, and attendee communication.

### Registration form

A configurable form used by attendees to register for an event.

### Attendee

A person who registers for or attends an event.

### Registration

The act or record of signing up for an event.

### Registration status

The current state of an attendee registration, such as invited, registered, confirmed, waiting list, cancelled, or declined where relevant.

### Attendance status

Whether a registered attendee attended, checked in, did not attend, or participated online.

### Check-in

The process of registering an attendee’s arrival at a physical event.

### Check-in app

The mobile app used to scan or register attendees on-site.

### Badge solution

A feature or process used to support attendee identification during physical events.

### Plus-one

An additional guest registered together with a main attendee.

### Waiting list

A list of people waiting for a place when event capacity is limited.

### Ticket

A registration-based access item for paid or controlled events.

### Ticket type

A category of ticket, such as standard, VIP, member, online, physical, early bird, or another event-specific type.

### Payment status

The payment state linked to a paid event registration or ticket.

### Invitation

An event email inviting someone to register or attend.

### Confirmation email

An email confirming a registration.

### Reminder email

An email reminding attendees of event details before the event.

### Access information

Information needed to attend an online or hybrid event, such as streaming link or joining instructions.

### Online attendee

An attendee participating remotely.

### Physical attendee

An attendee attending on-site.

### Hybrid event

An event with both physical and online attendees.

### Event record

The complete data record of the event, including setup, registrations, communications, attendance, and insights.

